      "message": "I believe that with the multithreading guarantees (that no two calls mutating the state of the buffer are allowed concurrently), this should work:\n\n```\n// Leave the buffer in an unmapped state if finalizing the mapping fails. We\u0027ll have a device loss anyway.\nmState.store(BufferState::Unmapped, std::memory_order::release);\nDAWN_TRY(FinalizeMapImpl(newState));\n\n    if (mStagingBuffer) {\n        mMappedPointer \u003d mStagingBuffer-\u003eGetMappedPointerImpl();\n    } else if (GetSize() \u003d\u003d 0) {\n        mMappedPointer \u003d static_cast\u003cvoid*\u003e(\u0026sZeroSizedMappingData);\n    } else {\n        mMappedPointer \u003d GetMappedPointerImpl();\n    }\n\n    mState.store(newState, std::memory_order::release);\n    return {};\n```",
